Subject: [PATCH] fix(capture): gather hidden states across hosts before
 slicing them

With --nnodes above 1, logits_output.hidden_states is a global array whose
rows can sit on devices other processes own, and the scheduler's slice for
each request raises a ShardingTypeError. Every rank processes the same batch
in the same order, so _rows_to_slice runs one process_allgather per batch and
every request slices the host copy. A single-host engine keeps its fully
addressable array unchanged.
---
 .../srt/managers/scheduler_output_processor_mixin.py  | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/python/sgl_jax/srt/managers/scheduler_output_processor_mixin.py b/python/sgl_jax/srt/managers/scheduler_output_processor_mixin.py
index 68cfe56d..31ce3d41 100644
--- a/python/sgl_jax/srt/managers/scheduler_output_processor_mixin.py
+++ b/python/sgl_jax/srt/managers/scheduler_output_processor_mixin.py
@@ -100,7 +100,16 @@ def _rows_to_slice(hidden_states, dp_size):
     request, so the batch's rows come to the host once. At one rank each request slices its
     own rows on the device, which moves no padding rows.
     """
-    if hidden_states is None or dp_size <= 1:
+    if hidden_states is None:
+        return None
+    if not getattr(hidden_states, "is_fully_addressable", True):
+        # With --nnodes above 1 the rows can sit on devices other processes own. Every rank
+        # processes the same batch in the same order, so one process_allgather puts the whole
+        # batch on every host.
+        from jax.experimental import multihost_utils
+
+        return np.asarray(multihost_utils.process_allgather(hidden_states, tiled=True))
+    if dp_size <= 1:
         return hidden_states
     return np.asarray(jax.device_get(hidden_states))
 
